decision: changes-requested

One medium blocker remains in R2’s regression guard. The three production readers correctly reject trailing content, and the focused regression suite passed.

**F1 — medium, blocker:** [strict_json_test.go:95](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3488747883/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/strict_json_test.go:95) treats `Decode(new(T))` as proof of an end check. A reader containing `DisallowUnknownFields(); return dec.Decode(new(Config))` therefore passes the guard while accepting trailing JSON. Lines 90–91 also accept `More()`, which returns false for trailing `}` or `]` without establishing EOF. Require a checked end condition and add negative fixtures for these cases.

Applied the review workflow and backend-Go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules. Reviewed bundle `rvb-86557565efa7bcaf` against R1, R2, and D1.

The artifact gate passed with 956 warnings and no blocking findings; the surface gate reported no findings. Full validation uses the sealed pipeline evidence. An additional in-memory probe could not compile because the sandbox refused Go’s build directory; F1 follows directly from the guard and the installed Go implementation. No repository files were changed or attestation recorded.

